WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.083 --> 00:00:15.809
On August 12, 2020,

00:00:15.833 --> 00:00:19.268
two groups of girls
went out to protest in Minsk,

00:00:19.292 --> 00:00:21.726
the capital city of Belarus.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.434
They put on white clothes

00:00:23.458 --> 00:00:26.000
and went barefoot out into the street.

00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:28.101
In the morning,

00:00:28.125 --> 00:00:31.601
some went to Komarovskiy Market
in the center of town.

00:00:31.625 --> 00:00:32.893
Later that day,

00:00:32.917 --> 00:00:35.226
the other group gathered with flowers

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.809
at the eternal flame
under the victory monument.

00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:41.143
They stood together holding hands,

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:44.476
and they started to sing
the Belarusian lullaby,

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.333
waiting for the police cars to arrive.

00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:52.393
They knew the police
would pick them up just like that:

00:00:52.417 --> 00:00:55.476
barefoot with flowers in their hands,

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.726
that they would take them
to the police station,

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.083
beat them up and try to humiliate them.

00:01:02.958 --> 00:01:05.625
And yet they did it anyway.

00:01:06.542 --> 00:01:09.434
This year, something changed in Belarus,

00:01:09.458 --> 00:01:12.601
a country of more than nine million people

00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:16.958
that has been ruled
by an authoritarian leader since 1994.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:23.268
These young women were protesting
the latest rigged election result,

00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:25.750
which had taken [place] 
just a few days earlier.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.643
Their small expressions of protest
very quickly expanded

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:35.893
into massive, peaceful,
women-led demonstrations

00:01:35.917 --> 00:01:37.375
all across the country.

00:01:38.417 --> 00:01:40.351
Within just a few days,

00:01:40.375 --> 00:01:43.768
a few hundred thousand people
took to the streets

00:01:43.792 --> 00:01:47.559
and demonstrations
have continued ever since,

00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:51.208
the likes of which
Belarus has never seen before.

00:01:52.208 --> 00:01:54.726
All this despite the fact

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:58.393
that the president proclaimed
himself reelected

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:02.184
and that more than 10,000 people
have been detained,

00:02:02.208 --> 00:02:04.059
hundreds tortured

00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:06.208
and at least six killed.

00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:12.851
Many people wonder why the people
of Belarus are speaking up now.

00:02:12.875 --> 00:02:16.476
What makes them keep taking to the streets

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.518
despite unprecedented police violence,

00:02:19.542 --> 00:02:21.708
despite state lawlessness?

00:02:22.958 --> 00:02:25.143
The answer I hear the most

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:27.958
is that people have become fearless,

00:02:29.333 --> 00:02:32.375
and it's something
we have become together.

00:02:33.625 --> 00:02:38.101
Because fear is the province of one.

00:02:38.125 --> 00:02:40.643
It feeds on isolation.

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:42.434
It doesn't discriminate:

00:02:42.458 --> 00:02:45.434
men, women, children, elderly --

00:02:45.458 --> 00:02:47.726
all of us can feel fear,

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:51.208
but only as long as we are on our own.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:55.101
Fearlessness takes two.

00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:59.208
It only works if and when
we show up for each other.

00:03:00.125 --> 00:03:02.434
Show up so that your neighbor,

00:03:02.458 --> 00:03:05.292
your colleague, your friend has courage.

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:08.542
And they will do the same for you.

00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:14.059
A lot has been made of my own role
in the presidential election

00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:16.184
of August 2020.

00:03:16.208 --> 00:03:20.226
How I stepped in to run for my husband,
Sergei, when he was jailed

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:25.934
and it became clear that the authorities
would deny him his chance to run himself;

00:03:25.958 --> 00:03:27.976
how I rightfully won the election

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.268
and became the elected leader
of a democratic Belarus,

00:03:31.292 --> 00:03:35.059
but the official results
only gave me 10 percent of the vote

00:03:35.083 --> 00:03:39.143
and I was forced
into exile with my children;

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:42.143
how I still fight
for those who voted for me

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:45.351
and whose voice the regime wants to steal;

00:03:45.375 --> 00:03:47.500
how "fearless" I am.

00:03:48.875 --> 00:03:52.684
But there were many moments
when I was frightened,

00:03:52.708 --> 00:03:55.184
and I wanted to step down.

00:03:55.208 --> 00:03:56.476
I was threatened

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:00.083
and forced to believe
that I'm alone in this fight.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:04.226
And yet the more cities I visited,

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.809
the more people showed up for the rallies,

00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:09.268
the less fear I had.

00:04:09.292 --> 00:04:12.601
And then in the days
before the election in Minsk,

00:04:12.625 --> 00:04:16.809
60,000 people came
to show their support for me,

00:04:16.833 --> 00:04:19.583
and I was no longer afraid.

00:04:20.917 --> 00:04:23.601
I never wanted to do any of this.

00:04:23.625 --> 00:04:25.476
I was never overly political,

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.934
and I never planned to run for office.

00:04:27.958 --> 00:04:30.583
I wanted to be a mom and a wife.

00:04:31.542 --> 00:04:34.518
But by fate and the will of my people,

00:04:34.542 --> 00:04:37.167
I was elevated to this position.

00:04:38.208 --> 00:04:42.208
And I accept this
with a sense of duty and pride.

00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:44.833
I will not give up.

00:04:45.625 --> 00:04:49.833
And I will show up for people,
because they show up for me.

00:04:50.875 --> 00:04:53.333
Our courage is born from unity.

00:04:54.333 --> 00:04:57.208
Our solidarity is our strength.

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:03.559
I also now understand
that being fearless is a commitment.

00:05:03.583 --> 00:05:07.226
It is a decision you make
every single day.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:09.934
It is a responsibility you take --

00:05:09.958 --> 00:05:13.184
responsibility for one another.

00:05:13.208 --> 00:05:17.643
In this regard, I'm no different
from my fellow Belarusians.

00:05:17.667 --> 00:05:20.184
Their support is tangible.

00:05:20.208 --> 00:05:23.976
Their solidarity grows in progression.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.768
When there are two of you,

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:27.518
you are daring.

00:05:27.542 --> 00:05:29.875
When you're 100, you are brave.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.851
When there are thousands of you,

00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:34.559
you are fearless.

00:05:34.583 --> 00:05:37.559
And once you are tens of thousands,

00:05:37.583 --> 00:05:40.393
you become invincible.

00:05:40.417 --> 00:05:41.667
Thank you.

